{"id": "EUVD-2026-103318", "enisaUuid": "b4e5601e-5e2c-3d5e-b0c4-f97d0120fa3d", "description": "phpMyFAQ 4.2.0-alpha before 4.2.0-beta contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in isFaqAccessibleForUser() that treats a missing FAQ translation as visible to unauthenticated users. Attackers can send a mismatched Accept-Language header to the comments and attachments API endpoints to read comments and attachment listings of unpublished or ACL-restricted FAQs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:39:57", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-g6fj-8cjr-wrxv", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-4.2.0-alpha-before-4.2.0-beta-authorization-bypass-via-comments-and-attachments-api"], "aliases": ["GHSA-346r-939v-qh8c", "CVE-2026-111902"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d61f4afc-7fd4-3e91-a201-b13e385e3211", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0-alpha <4.2.0-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "49884fa8-b6b0-307f-b88b-5fb8c08eb612", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}